I do want to say... that
I know that this has been hard


01:24:59.239 --> 01:25:03.828
for you not being able
to have... the doorstep...


01:25:05.371 --> 01:25:11.461
but the privacy that it afforded me
was wonderful for me today.


01:25:17.175 --> 01:25:19.574
I think it's thrilling.
I stopped everything, and watched it,


01:25:19.636 --> 01:25:22.305
and the baby was watching it,
and she wanted to go too.


01:25:22.430 --> 01:25:26.266
She's four years old, and she wanted
to go on the trip with the, with the man.


01:25:26.350 --> 01:25:28.978
And when his children and his wife
were on, uh,


01:25:30.020 --> 01:25:31.605
I thought it was real exciting.


01:25:32.439 --> 01:25:35.234
I think everybody was more or less
sitting on the edge


01:25:35.318 --> 01:25:37.153
of their seats until they did find him.


01:25:37.235 --> 01:25:40.948
I think it's wonderful. I think
it's a great thing for this country!


01:25:41.157 --> 01:25:43.451
And believe me,
we're never going to be buried.


01:25:55.462 --> 01:25:57.881
<i>Roger, Wally,
you got anything to say to everyone</i>


01:25:57.965 --> 01:25:59.765
<i>watching you across the country
on this thing?</i>


01:25:59.801 --> 01:26:01.051
<i>We're going out live on this.</i>


01:26:02.177 --> 01:26:04.305
<i>I'm looking at the United States,</i>


01:26:05.014 --> 01:26:07.684
<i>and starting to pitch up slightly
with this drifting rate.</i>


01:26:08.266 --> 01:26:11.270
<i>And I see the Moon, which I'm sure no one
in the United States can see</i>


01:26:11.354 --> 01:26:12.771
<i>as well as I right now.</i>


01:26:26.159 --> 01:26:29.788
<i>This flight's scheduled
to be the last of the Mercury Program</i>


01:26:29.872 --> 01:26:32.750
<i>before the Mercury Program ends,
and we begin flights</i>


01:26:32.958 --> 01:26:35.420
<i>in our two-man capsule, the Gemini.</i>


01:26:35.545 --> 01:26:39.381
<i>The intermediate step before we go
to Apollo, and the step to the Moon.</i>


01:26:43.344 --> 01:26:46.555
<i>America's team of astronauts
was increased to 16 today,</i>


01:26:48.099 --> 01:26:51.476
<i>when The Manned Space Center at Houston,
Texas named the men today.</i>


01:26:51.644 --> 01:26:55.273
<i>It was specified that they will be trained
for trips to the Moon.</i>


01:26:58.943 --> 01:27:00.194
We've had a number of these...


01:27:01.028 --> 01:27:03.864
ceremonies at the White House
and at Cape Canaveral to pay tribute


01:27:04.731 --> 01:27:07.118
to a very distinguished group
of Americans, who have in,


01:27:07.452 --> 01:27:12.206
our time, in this rather civil society,
demonstrated that there are...


01:27:13.039 --> 01:27:15.001
<i>great frontiers still to be crossed.</i>


01:27:15.626 --> 01:27:19.588
<i>And in flying through space, they've
carried with them the wishes, the prayers,</i>


01:27:19.713 --> 01:27:23.176
<i>the hopes and the pride of 180 million
of their fellow countrymen.</i>


01:27:26.470 --> 01:27:29.974
<i>I hope that, uh, we will be encouraged
to continue with this program.</i>


01:27:30.640 --> 01:27:33.060
<i>I know that a good many people
say, "Why go to the Moon?"</i>


01:27:33.394 --> 01:27:36.354
<i>Just as many people said
to Lindbergh, "Why go to Paris?"</i>


01:27:39.317 --> 01:27:42.444
Lindbergh said, "It's not so much a matter
of logic as it is of feeling."


01:27:47.324 --> 01:27:50.328
<i>I think that the United States has
committed itself to this great adventure</i>


01:27:50.411 --> 01:27:53.997
<i>in the '60s. I think before the end
of the '60s, we will see a man</i>


01:27:54.081 --> 01:27:55.500
<i>on the Moon, an American.</i>


01:27:55.875 --> 01:27:59.045
<i>And I think in so doing, it's not nearly
that we're interested in making</i>


01:27:59.127 --> 01:28:02.631
<i>this particular journey, but we are
interested in demonstrating</i>


01:28:02.756 --> 01:28:04.966
<i>a dominance of this new sea,</i>


01:28:05.592 --> 01:28:08.762
<i>and making sure that
in this new great adventurous period,</i>


01:28:09.262 --> 01:28:13.309
<i>that the Americans are playing
their great role as they have in the past.</i>

